@startuml
title Sequence Diagram: Submitting an Ownership Claim

autonumber
actor "Claimant Student" as Claimant
participant "ClaimItemPage" as UI
participant "Storage Service" as Storage
participant "Supabase Storage\n(private 'claim-evidence')" as PrivBucket
participant "PostgreSQL DB\n(claims & notifications)" as DB
actor "Original Finder" as Finder

Claimant -> UI: Open /items/:id/claim
UI -> DB: Query existing claim for (item_id, claimant_id)
DB --> UI: 0 rows (No prior active claim)

Claimant -> UI: Enter claim message & secret distinguishing details
Claimant -> UI: (Optional) Attach invoice or proof photo
UI -> UI: Validate inputs

Claimant -> UI: Click "Submit Claim for Review"
UI -> DB: INSERT into claims (item_id, claimant_id, claim_message, proof_details, status='pending_review')
DB --> UI: Return claim ID

alt Proof Photo Provided
    UI -> Storage: uploadClaimEvidence(file, claim.id)
    Storage -> PrivBucket: Upload to encrypted private bucket
    PrivBucket --> Storage: Path confirmed
    Storage --> UI: Return private evidence URL
    UI -> DB: UPDATE claims SET proof_photo_url = url WHERE id = claim.id
    DB --> UI: Confirmed
end

UI -> DB: INSERT into notifications (user_id = item.reported_by, title="New Claim Filed", type="new_claim")
DB --> Finder: Real-time notification delivered

UI -> Claimant: Redirect to /dashboard with success toast: "Claim under review"

@enduml
